{% extends '_layout/app.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'settings.title'|trans }} — {{ 'app.name'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{#
A saved setting redraws the page in place instead of reloading it.

Every control here posts and is redirected back to its own section, and Turbo
treats a redirect to the page you are on as a refresh. With these two tags that
refresh is a MORPH that keeps the scroll position: the card you changed, the
flash and the sidebar beside it all update where they are, and the page neither
blanks nor jumps to the top. Before this every form opted out of Turbo with
data-turbo="false", so one click on a checkbox reloaded the whole document and
dropped the reader back at the top of a long section.

Morph rather than a Turbo Stream per control: one rule for all thirty-odd
forms, and a form added later gets it for nothing. A control whose effect is
somewhere the server renders — the sidebar for Settings → General → Layout & controls,
the times for the clock — is right after the redirect because the whole page
was rendered again; a stream would have to know every place it shows.

A few still reload on purpose and keep data-turbo="false": the language,
because every string on the page and <html lang> change with it; the 12/24-hour
clock, because it is published on <html> and a morph only reaches <body>; and
the links that leave the app (a provider's consent screen, an .ics download).
#}
{% block turbo_refresh %}
    <meta name="turbo-refresh-method" content="morph">
    <meta name="turbo-refresh-scroll" content="preserve">
{% endblock %}
{# No override any more. This one existed to drop mail--mail-pane, and named
   `mercure` — an identifier that stopped existing when the controllers were
   grouped into directories, so settings pages have had no live updates since.
   The default is core--mercure alone, which is what this page wanted. #}
{% block body %}
    <div class="h-full overflow-hidden app-bg"
         data-controller="ui--sidebar-drawer">

        {# Mobile backdrop #}
        <div data-ui--sidebar-drawer-target="backdrop" data-action="click->ui--sidebar-drawer#backdropClick"
             class="md:hidden fixed inset-0 z-30 bg-black/40 backdrop-blur-sm opacity-0 pointer-events-none transition-opacity duration-200"
             aria-hidden="true"></div>

        {# Mobile sidebar drawer #}
        <div data-ui--sidebar-drawer-target="drawer" id="sidebar-drawer" inert
             class="md:hidden fixed inset-y-0 left-0 z-40 w-64 p-3 -translate-x-full transition-transform duration-200 ease-out">
            {% include '_partials/_sidebar.html.twig' with { _drawerMode: true } %}
        </div>

        <div class="shell-frame flex h-full flex-col p-gutter gap-gutter">

            {% include '_partials/_topbar.html.twig' %}

            <div class="flex flex-1 gap-gutter overflow-hidden">

                {# Sidebar — desktop #}
                <div class="hidden md:flex">
                    {% include '_partials/_sidebar.html.twig' %}
                </div>

                {# Main content pane — settings #}
                <div class="flex flex-1 overflow-hidden main-pane">
                    <div class="flex flex-col flex-1 overflow-hidden">

                        {# Pane header #}
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 px-6 h-14 border-b border-line shrink-0">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-gear text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <h1 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'settings.title'|trans }}</h1>
                        </div>

                        {# Scrollable body: section nav + content.
                           IMPORTANT: this grid must have exactly TWO children —
                           the nav and ONE content wrapper. A third child wraps
                           into the 180px nav column on the next grid row.

                           `relative` so this port, not .shell-frame, is what
                           absolutely positioned content is placed against and
                           clipped by. Without it the sr-only labels of Compose
                           defaults (one per address) sat where they would have
                           been without the port, far below the window, and made
                           the clipped shell scrollable: a search result's
                           scroll then moved the whole page up, top bar and
                           all, with no scrollbar to put it back. #}
                        <div class="relative flex-1 overflow-y-auto @container
                                    {{ 'appearance' == section ? 'pane-fill-port' : '' }}">
                            {# `pane-fill-host` for Appearance only, and this is the
                               one line that decides whether that section GROWS this
                               scroll port or FILLS it.

                               Every other section is a stack of cards that gets as
                               long as it gets and scrolls here. Appearance is two
                               peer cards beside a draggable boundary, and a boundary
                               is only a boundary if both sides are the same height —
                               so it takes the port's height instead of setting it,
                               and each card scrolls its own body the way .main-pane
                               does. See the block in app.css: above 80rem it caps
                               the row, below it every rule is inert and this class
                               does nothing at all.

                               Naming the section here rather than letting the
                               included template ask for it, because it is this
                               element's height that is being given away and this is
                               where a reader looks for what happened to it. #}
                            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-6 px-6 py-6
                                        {{ 'appearance' == section ? 'pane-fill-host' : '' }}">

                                {# The tree — areas, pages and a filter over every card
                                   (#569). It replaced five groups over twenty-nine flat
                                   links; settings/_nav.html.twig says why, and
                                   SettingsNavigation holds the table it draws. #}
                                {% include 'settings/_nav.html.twig' %}

                                {# Single content wrapper — second (and last) grid child.

                                   The negative margin cancels the wrapper's px-6 for this
                                   child only, so the section cards run to the pane's edges
                                   and their own px-4 is the single inset left. Nesting
                                   a card inside a padded page cost 40px a side otherwise,
                                   which on a 360px screen is spent before any content. The
                                   nav keeps its padding: it is the other grid child and
                                   reads as chrome rather than as a card. Restored above
                                   42rem of pane, where the space is not scarce and a card
                                   flush to the edge only looks unfinished.

                                   Container query rather than a breakpoint, for the reason
                                   the admin page documents: this pane is not as wide as the
                                   window, and at md the mail sidebar appears and takes from
                                   it, so pane width and viewport width do not move
                                   together.

                                   THERE ARE NO `px-4 @2xl:px-0` PAYBACK WRAPPERS LEFT IN
                                   HERE, and that is the rule finishing rather than an
                                   exception to it. The payback existed for content that was
                                   not a card — a bare heading over a bordered box — which
                                   the `-mx-6` would have pushed flush against the pane
                                   border and clipped. Every section is a real card now, its
                                   heading inside its own header band, so every section is
                                   the case the `-mx-6` was written for and paying it back
                                   would inset one card 16px further than its neighbour.
                                   If you add a section that is NOT a card, it pays.

                                   One section still does: health renders a FEED of
                                   per-issue cards rather than a single card, so its
                                   heading is not a card header and pays the -mx-6 back
                                   inside settings/_health.html.twig, where the reason
                                   is written out. #}
                                <div class="min-w-0 -mx-6 @2xl:mx-0
                                            {{ 'appearance' == section ? 'pane-fill pane-fill-stack' : '' }}">
                                    {% if section == 'health' %}
                                        {% include 'settings/_health.html.twig' %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'appearance' %}
                                        {# The one section that is not the generic card, and
                                           deliberately so: it is also the setup wizard's
                                           appearance step, it carries its own @container,
                                           its two cards are a split pair with a resizable
                                           handle between them, and its controls card scrolls
                                           its own body under a capped row. It draws the same
                                           chrome from _partials/_card_chrome.html.twig, so it
                                           matches without being flattened into the macro. #}
                                        {% include 'settings/_appearance.html.twig' %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'profile' %}
                                        {% include 'settings/_profile.html.twig' %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'security' %}
                                        {# Two peer cards: the password, then the
                                           second factor. The wrapping div is not
                                           decoration — it is the Turbo Stream
                                           target the change endpoint replaces,
                                           so the id has to survive here and in
                                           settings/_password.stream.html.twig
                                           identically. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            <div id="settings-password">
                                                {% include 'settings/_password.html.twig' %}
                                            </div>
                                            {% include 'settings/_security.html.twig' %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'region' %}
                                        {# Language & region: what used to open the General page,
                                           without the compose, sidebar and what's-new cards that
                                           had nowhere better to go and now do (#569).

                                           Three peer cards, not one card with three bands:
                                           language, zone and clock are each a section-grade
                                           subject with its own heading AND subheading in the
                                           catalogue. That is the rule this page follows —
                                           groups that merely partition one subject's list
                                           stay inside a single card as h3 bands. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-language',
                                                heading:    'settings.language.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.language.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_language.html.twig' with {
                                                        locales: locales,
                                                        activeLocale: activeLocale,
                                                    } %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-timezone',
                                                heading:    'settings.timezone.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.timezone.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_timezone.html.twig' with {
                                                        timezoneGroups: timezoneGroups,
                                                        activeTimezone: activeTimezone,
                                                        defaultTimezone: defaultTimezone,
                                                        currentTime: currentTime,
                                                    } %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {# Under the zone rather than beside the language: the two
                                               together answer "what time is it, and how is it
                                               written", and somebody fixing one has usually come to
                                               fix the other. #}
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-clock',
                                                heading:    'settings.clock.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.clock.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_clock.html.twig' with {
                                                        clockOptions: clockOptions,
                                                        activeClock: activeClock,
                                                        defaultClock: defaultClock,
                                                        clockPlacements: clockPlacements,
                                                        activeClockPlacement: activeClockPlacement,
                                                    } %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'whats-new' %}
                                        {# Its own page: the way back from "Don't show this after
                                           updates" in the dialog itself (#165), and a link the dialog
                                           can name without sending people to the bottom of General. #}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-whats-new',
                                            heading:    'settings.whats_new.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.whats_new.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {% include 'settings/_whats_new.html.twig' with {
                                                    show: not app.user.whatsNewQuiet,
                                                } %}
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'layout' %}
                                        {# How the app is driven rather than how it looks: which
                                           folders the sidebar shows, what a swipe does, and the
                                           keyboard. Each was a page or a stray card of its own. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-sidebar',
                                                heading:    'settings.sidebar.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.sidebar.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_sidebar_more.html.twig' %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-swipe-actions',
                                                heading:    'settings.swipe_actions.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.swipe_actions.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_swipe_actions.html.twig' with {
                                                        choices: swipeChoices,
                                                        right:   app.user.swipeRightAction,
                                                        left:    app.user.swipeLeftAction,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-shortcuts',
                                                heading:    'settings.shortcuts.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.shortcuts.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_shortcuts.html.twig' with {
                                                        enabled: app.user.keyboardShortcuts,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'reading' %}
                                        {# What happens when a mail is opened: where it opens, and
                                           whether its remote images load. Two one-card pages before. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-reading-pane',
                                                heading:    'settings.reading_pane.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.reading_pane.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_reading_pane.html.twig' with {
                                                        mode: app.user.readingPaneMode,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-images',
                                                heading:    'settings.images.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.images.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_images.html.twig' with {
                                                        alwaysShow: app.user.alwaysShowImages,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'compose' %}
                                        {# What happens when a mail is written. Compose behaviour came
                                           from General; read receipts were a page of their own, named
                                           after the thing they configure, and still are a card of
                                           their own here — per alias, because a receipt policy is a
                                           property of the address you send from. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-compose-behaviour',
                                                heading:    'settings.compose_behavior.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.compose_behavior.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_compose_behavior.html.twig' with {
                                                        forwardQuoteCollapsed: forwardQuoteCollapsed,
                                                    } %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-read-receipts',
                                                heading:    'settings.compose_defaults.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.compose_defaults.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    <div id="settings-compose-defaults">
                                                        {% include 'settings/_compose_defaults.html.twig' with {
                                                            manageableAccounts: manageableAccounts,
                                                        } %}
                                                    </div>
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'message-list' %}
                                        {# What a row in the list shows (#608). Five of these
                                           were a group on Appearance; the page is its own
                                           because they say what a row tells you, not how
                                           the app looks. #}
                                        {% include 'settings/_message_list.html.twig' %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'categories' %}
                                        {# Everything about the inbox tabs on one page: what sorts
                                           mail into them, then the tabs themselves — which built-in
                                           ones are on, the reader's own, and the order of all of
                                           them. The sorting card used to sit under General, and the
                                           tabs it sorts into were a second card beside it. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-sorting',
                                                heading:    'settings.sorting.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.sorting.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_sorting.html.twig' with {
                                                        source:           app.user.categorySorting.source,
                                                        overrideProvider: app.user.categorySorting.overrideProvider,
                                                        assistantOffered: ai_categorisation_enabled(),
                                                        tabs:             app.user.categorySorting.tabs,
                                                        accountTabs:      app.user.accountInboxTabs,
                                                    } %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-inbox-tabs',
                                                heading:    'settings.categories.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.categories.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_inbox_tabs.html.twig' with {
                                                        tabs:        categoryTabs,
                                                        switchedOff: app.user.categorySorting.switchedOff(),
                                                    } %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {# The number beside each tab's name. Stored with the
                                               message list settings (#608) and set here, beside the
                                               tabs it counts, by the same controller and endpoint. #}
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-tab-counts',
                                                heading:    'settings.message_list.tab_counts.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.message_list.tab_counts.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_tab_counts.html.twig' %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'inboxes' %}
                                        {# The unified inboxes (#265): the inboxes themselves,
                                           then which one each account is listed in. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-unified-inboxes',
                                                heading:    'settings.unified_inboxes.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.unified_inboxes.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_unified_inboxes.html.twig' with {
                                                        inboxes: unifiedInboxes,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-unified-inbox-accounts',
                                                heading:    'settings.unified_inboxes.accounts_heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.unified_inboxes.accounts_subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_unified_inbox_accounts.html.twig' with {
                                                        inboxes:  unifiedInboxes,
                                                        accounts: manageableAccounts,
                                                        inboxOf:  inboxOfAccount,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'encryption' %}
                                        {# Its own cards, like security: four subjects, not one. #}
                                        {% include 'settings/_encryption.html.twig' %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'calendar-behaviour' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-calendar-behaviour',
                                            heading:    'settings.calendar_behaviour.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.calendar_behaviour.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {% include 'settings/_calendar_behaviour.html.twig' with {
                                                    skip: app.user.calendarSwitchSkip,
                                                } only %}
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'disposal' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-disposal',
                                            heading:    'settings.disposal.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.disposal.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {% include 'settings/_disposal.html.twig' with {
                                                    deleteNow: app.user.deleteNowButtons,
                                                } only %}
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'aliases' %}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-aliases',
                                                heading:    'settings.aliases.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.aliases.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    <div id="settings-alias-list">
                                                        {% include 'settings/_aliases.html.twig' with {
                                                            manageableAccounts: manageableAccounts,
                                                            aliasForms: aliasForms,
                                                        } %}
                                                    </div>
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                        </div>
                                    {% elseif section == 'signature' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-signature',
                                            heading:    'settings.signature.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.signature.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                <div id="settings-signature">
                                                    {% include 'settings/_signature.html.twig' with {
                                                        manageableAccounts: manageableAccounts,
                                                    } %}
                                                </div>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'templates' %}
                                        {# ONE card holding both the tree and the editor, where
                                           filters put the editor in a second card below the
                                           list. A filter is edited and left; a template is
                                           written, and a tree beside the page being written is
                                           how every editor with folders looks. #}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-templates',
                                            heading:    'settings.templates.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.templates.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {% include 'settings/_templates.html.twig' with { tree: templateTree } only %}
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}
                                    {% elseif section == 'filters' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-filters',
                                            heading:    'settings.filters.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.filters.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {# A frame, so a run in progress can re-read itself without
                                                   a full navigation. Its src is the same partial the stream
                                                   replaces, so both paths render one template. The frame is
                                                   no longer the card — it is the card's body, so the list
                                                   and the heading above it are one surface. #}
                                                <turbo-frame id="settings-filter-frame"
                                                             src="{{ path('app_settings_filters_list') }}"
                                                             class="block">
                                                    <div id="settings-filter-list">
                                                        {% include 'settings/_filters.html.twig' with { rules: rules, labels: labels } %}
                                                    </div>
                                                </turbo-frame>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                        {# The editor opens below the list rather than replacing it, so the
                                           rule being edited stays visible next to its siblings. #}
                                        <div class="mt-4">
                                            {# Opened from a message ("Create a filter from this
                                               message"): the editor loads on that message's draft
                                               rather than waiting to be asked for. #}
                                            {% if filterFromMessage %}
                                                <turbo-frame id="filter-editor"
                                                             src="{{ path('app_settings_filters_new', { message: filterFromMessage }) }}"></turbo-frame>
                                            {% else %}
                                                {% include 'settings/filters/_editor_empty.html.twig' %}
                                            {% endif %}
                                        </div>

                                    {% elseif section == 'notifications' %}
                                        {# ONE card: the device list does not partition a
                                           different subject, it is what registering this
                                           browser has produced across every device. The
                                           toggle registers, the list below reports. #}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-notifications',
                                            heading:    'settings.notifications.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.notifications.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {% include 'settings/_notifications.html.twig' with {
                                                    vapidPublicKey: vapidPublicKey,
                                                } %}

                                                {% include 'settings/_notification_preferences.html.twig' with {
                                                    skipRead: app.user.notifySkipsRead,
                                                    chosen:   app.user.notifyScopes,
                                                    switches: notifySwitches,
                                                } %}

                                                {# Wrapped in an id because removing
                                                   a device replaces the whole list
                                                   over Turbo — see
                                                   push_device/_mutation.stream.html.twig. #}
                                                <div id="settings-push-device-list">
                                                    {% include 'settings/_push_devices.html.twig' with {
                                                        devices: pushDevices,
                                                        lastDeliveries: lastDeliveries,
                                                    } %}
                                                </div>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% elseif section == 'app-passwords' %}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-app-passwords',
                                                heading:    'settings.app_passwords.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.app_passwords.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    <div id="settings-app-password-list">
                                                        {% include 'settings/_app_passwords.html.twig' with {
                                                            apiTokens: apiTokens,
                                                            apiTokenForm: apiTokenForm,
                                                        } %}
                                                    </div>
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {# Its own card rather than a band in the one
                                               above: "where do I point my client" is a
                                               different question from "which passwords
                                               exist", and it has its own heading in the
                                               catalogue. Padded — it is prose, not a list. #}
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-app-setup',
                                                heading: 'settings.app_passwords.setup_heading'|trans,
                                                padded:  true,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                                                        {{ 'settings.app_passwords.setup_hint'|trans }}
                                                    </p>
                                                    <code class="mt-2 block break-all rounded-lg bg-zinc-500/10 px-3 py-2 text-[11px] font-mono text-ink select-all">{{ public_address() }}/jmap/session</code>
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>

                                    {% elseif section == 'integrations' %}
                                        {# ONE card. "Connected", "Available" and "Elsewhere"
                                           partition a single list by state — they are not
                                           three subjects — so they are h3 bands inside the
                                           body rather than three peer cards. #}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-integrations',
                                            heading:    'settings.integrations.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.integrations.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {# Loaded through its own frame rather than rendered inline:
                                                   every mutation replaces the frame, and the connect form
                                                   posts a Turbo Stream that needs a stable target. #}
                                                <turbo-frame id="settings-integrations-frame"
                                                             src="{{ path('app_settings_integrations_list') }}"
                                                             loading="lazy"
                                                             class="block">
                                                    <div class="py-10 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint">
                                                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin mr-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ 'admin.loading'|trans }}
                                                    </div>
                                                </turbo-frame>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% elseif section == 'ai' %}
                                        {# Three peer cards of its own, so the include
                                           carries the whole section rather than one card
                                           body — unlike insights below, which is a single
                                           list inside a single card. #}
                                        {% include 'settings/_ai.html.twig' with {
                                            aiFeatures:     aiFeatures,
                                            aiReplyContext: aiReplyContext,
                                            aiAboutMe:      aiAboutMe,
                                            aiSystemPrompt: aiSystemPrompt,
                                        } %}

                                    {% elseif section == 'insights' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-insights',
                                            heading:    'settings.insights.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.insights.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {% include 'settings/_insights.html.twig' with {
                                                    insightExtractors: insightExtractors,
                                                } %}
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% elseif section == 'labels' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-labels',
                                            heading:    'settings.labels.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.labels.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                <div id="settings-label-list">
                                                    {% include 'settings/_labels.html.twig' with { labels: labels } %}
                                                </div>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% elseif section == 'sharing' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-sharing',
                                            heading:    'settings.sharing.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.sharing.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {# The stream's target, re-emitted inside its own
                                                   replacement for the reason the calendar list
                                                   below states. Both halves of the section live
                                                   inside it, so creating a booking page redraws
                                                   the links too and neither can go stale behind
                                                   the other. #}
                                                <div id="settings-sharing-list">
                                                    {% include 'settings/sharing/_lists.html.twig' with {
                                                        shareLinks: shareLinks|default([]),
                                                        bookingPages: bookingPages|default([]),
                                                        mintedLinkUrl: null,
                                                        mintedBookingUrl: null,
                                                    } only %}
                                                </div>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% elseif section == 'contacts' %}
                                        {# Two cards, so the gap between them, as every two-card section has. #}
                                        <div class="space-y-4">
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-contacts',
                                                heading:    'settings.contacts.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.contacts.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {# The stream's target, re-emitted inside each
                                                       replacement — see the calendars block below. #}
                                                    <div id="settings-contacts-list">
                                                        {% include 'settings/_contacts.html.twig' with {
                                                            contactConnections: contactConnections|default([]),
                                                            addressBooks: addressBooks|default({}),
                                                            contactAccounts: contactAccounts|default([]),
                                                            accountBooks: accountBooks|default({}),
                                                            contactAccountsGranted: contactAccountsGranted|default({}),
                                                        } only %}
                                                    </div>
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}

                                            {# The contacts button's steps, under the address
                                               book's own section rather than a section of its
                                               own like the calendar's: one choice did not earn
                                               a row in the nav. #}
                                            {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                                id:         'card-contacts-behaviour',
                                                heading:    'settings.contacts_behaviour.heading'|trans,
                                                subheading: 'settings.contacts_behaviour.subheading'|trans,
                                            } %}
                                                {% block body %}
                                                    {% include 'settings/_contacts_behaviour.html.twig' with {
                                                        skip: app.user.contactsSwitchSkip,
                                                    } only %}
                                                {% endblock %}
                                            {% endembed %}
                                        </div>

                                    {% elseif section == 'calendars' %}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-calendars',
                                            heading:    'settings.calendars.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.calendars.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block body %}
                                                {# The id is the stream's target, so it wraps the
                                                   partial here and is re-emitted inside the
                                                   replacement — a replace that dropped it would
                                                   work once and then never again. #}
                                                <div id="settings-calendar-list">
                                                    {% include 'settings/_calendars.html.twig' with {
                                                        calendars: calendars,
                                                        calendarAccounts: calendarAccounts|default([]),
                                                        calendarConnections: calendarConnections|default([]),
                                                    } only %}
                                                </div>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% else %}
                                        {# The Add button rides in the header band via the
                                           card's `actions` block — the reason this is an
                                           embed and not a macro. #}
                                        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
                                            id:         'card-accounts',
                                            heading:    'settings.accounts.heading'|trans,
                                            subheading: 'settings.accounts.subheading'|trans,
                                        } %}
                                            {% block actions %}
                                                <button
                                                    type="button"
                                                    data-controller="ui--modal"
                                                    data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                                                    data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'sidebar.accounts.add'|trans }}"
                                                    data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_account_new') }}"
                                                    class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 h-9 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                                                           bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong text-accent-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                                                >
                                                    <i class="fa-solid fa-plus text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                    {{ 'sidebar.accounts.add'|trans }}
                                                </button>
                                            {% endblock %}

                                            {% block body %}
                                                <div id="settings-account-list">
                                                    {% include 'settings/_accounts.html.twig' with { manageableAccounts: manageableAccounts } %}
                                                </div>
                                            {% endblock %}
                                        {% endembed %}

                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>

                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
